{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib proof of the main results of Knowles and Yin, \"Anisotropic local laws for random matrices\" (arXiv:1410.3516). The sample covariance matrix is Q = T X X* T* with X an M x N matrix of independent centred real entries of variance 1/N (Assumption 2.1). Proved, for real matrices and real deterministic vectors, at fixed N >= N_0 with explicit constants: the anisotropic and averaged local laws (Theorem 3.6), the law outside the spectrum (Theorem 3.7), Corollary 3.9, the rigidity of the eigenvalues (Theorem 3.12), edge universality (Theorem 3.18), the local laws for general T (Proposition 11.1), and for deformed Wigner matrices the local laws (Theorem 12.2), the rigidity of the extreme eigenvalues (Theorem 12.4) and edge universality (Theorem 12.5). No result of another work is assumed for these statements; every result that the paper uses for them is proved in the library from Mathlib.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Jun Yin"
    }
  ],
